      "topics": [
        "csr-vs-ssr-vs-ssg",
        "nextjs-file-routing",
        "server-vs-client-components",
        "data-fetching-nextjs",
        "deploying-nextjs"
      ],
      "intro": "Next.js questions appear in fresher frontend interviews at product companies because most new React projects start with Next.js. Interviewers expect freshers to explain CSR vs SSR vs SSG (not just the acronyms \u2014 why each matters for SEO, TTFB, and data freshness), how Next.js file-based routing works (folders = routes, page.tsx convention, layout.tsx), the App Router's server vs client component model (why \"use client\" is needed and when to use it), basic data fetching in a Server Component using fetch with cache/revalidation options, and how to deploy to Vercel or a Node server. Knowing this distinguishes candidates who have built something real from those who only know create-react-app."
    }
